@@ -45,12 +45,20 @@ The current state is still monolithic, but the design aims for a microkernel arc
 
 ## Features
 
-- Minimal kernel: only scheduling, IPC, and memory management in kernel space
-- Message-based IPC for user-space servers
+- Ring-3 ELF user processes with `fork`, `exec`, `wait`, pipes and PTYs
+- Per-process working directories, descriptors, credentials and sessions
+- Message-based IPC and shared memory for user-space servers
 - Preemptive round-robin scheduler with priorities
 - Physical memory manager (bitmap allocator)
 - Kernel heap allocator
 - System calls via INT 0x80
+- User-space display server with managed windows and exclusive framebuffer ownership
+- Desktop top bar, clock, launcher, taskbar, Start/power menu, keyboard
+  shortcuts, and independently launchable terminal windows
+- User-space shell and core utilities without normal kernel-shell command dispatch
+- PS/2 pointing-device support; USB-HID and I2C-HID remain future hardware work
+
+See [docs/USERLAND.md](docs/USERLAND.md) for the desktop architecture.
 
 ## Building
 
